        move('the Sifrei 197:2-4 (read whole at the reading); MISHNAH SOTAH 8:5 (the exam row, read whole)', "MISHNAH SOTAH 8:5 — R. AKIVA: 'fearful and faint of heart' as it sounds, he cannot stand in the battle's ranks and see a drawn sword; R. YOSE THE GALILEAN: the fearful of the transgressions in his hand — and therefore the Torah hung all these others on him, that he return among them; R. YOSE: the widow to a high priest, the divorcee to a common priest, the mamzeret (a woman born of a forbidden union) to an Israelite — this is the fearful and faint of heart: THREE ARMS on the Mishnah's own row (197:2-4); 'lest his brothers' heart melt' — the fear contagious (197:4)")
